<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef generally lower on moderate demand and fairly heavy offerings. Select rib and chuck cuts steady to weak, while round and loin cuts weak. Choice cuts generally weak. Beef trimmings lower on fairly good demand and heavy offerings. - USDA</p>
<p>---</p>
<p>280 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p>105 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>32 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     107.76	107.51	102.18	101.10</p>
<p>Changes	  -1.10	 -1.07	 -0.84	 -0.74</p>
<p>Rib	  161.22	161.40	151.28	151.29</p>
<p>Chuck	 74.84	 72.49	 76.16	 72.60</p>
<p>Round	 94.13	 94.13	 89.65	 89.65</p>
<p>Loin	 173.51	175.49	154.96	154.83</p>
<p>Brisket     59.92	 59.92	 59.96	 59.96</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  68.24	 68.15	 68.49	 68.31</p>
<p>Flank	 59.62	 59.62	 60.33	 60.33</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
